# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS COMMITTED. This repo ships binaries — wheels for four
# platforms, an XCFramework, Android/iOS bundles — and a hybrid-signed build
# manifest; a signature over a build whose dependency graph nobody pinned
# attests to something that cannot be reproduced. Committing the lock also
# makes a dependency change a reviewable commit instead of a silent
# re-resolve on every CI run. (2026-09-03: tinyvec 1.13.0 published broken and
# took out every compiling job on `main` and on the v20.1.0 tag — including
# the artifact upload — on a tree that had been green minutes earlier.)
# Consumers are unaffected: cargo ignores a dependency's lockfile, so server
# and agent resolve their own.

